 ## Overview
-Cutaways are an illustrative volume rendering technique where occluding objects are removed to reveal the structure of interest [S1, book]. They solve the problem of visual obstruction in complex volumetric scenes by selectively suppressing background elements [S1, book]. Unlike ghosting, which reduces opacity to preserve spatial context, cutaways completely remove the occluding regions [S1, book].
