 4.  **Render:** Composite the remaining voxels using standard volume rendering techniques [G].
 
+**Formulas:**
+The output opacity $O_{\text{out}}(\mathbf{x})$ for a voxel $\mathbf{x}$ is computed as:
+$$
+O_{\text{out}}(\mathbf{x}) = 
+\begin{cases} 
+0 & \text{if } \mathbf{x} \in \text{Background} \land I(\mathbf{x}) > \tau \\
+O_{\text{orig}}(\mathbf{x}) & \text{otherwise}
+\end{cases}
+$$
+where $O_{\text{orig}}(\mathbf{x})$ is the original voxel opacity, $I(\mathbf{x})$ is the static importance value, and $\tau$ is a threshold controlling the cutaway boundary [S1, book].
+
 **Parameters:**
 *   **Importance Function:** Static definition used to skip costly compositing [S1, book].
 *   **Cutaway Degree:** The user can control the degree of cutaway, ranging from no cutaway (full background) to full cutaway (complete suppression of occluding structures) [S1, book].
-Typical parameter values are Not given in the sources.
