 ### Feature-Based Cut-Aways
-A technique to remove portions of Regions of Interest (ROIs) using axis-aligned, surface-aligned, or feature-based (segment-aligned) cuts [S2, unofficial]. It identifies obscuring features and applies cuts to remove them without impinging on ROI geometry [S2, unofficial]. What sets it apart from axis-aligned or surface-aligned cuts is its use of feature data to preserve ROI geometry [S2, unofficial]. Choose it when obscuring features must be removed without altering the target structure's shape [S2, unofficial]. See [Ghosting and Cutaway Techniques](8497-ghosting-and-cutaway-techniques.md) for related context-preserving methods.
